ai_circuit_breaker_transitions_total | counter | provider, state | internal/ai | AI provider circuit-breaker state transitions, by provider and new state (open/half-open/closed).
ai_request_duration_seconds | histogram | provider | internal/ai | AI provider request latency (a full Chat call or the lifetime of a Stream), by provider.
ai_request_errors_total | counter | provider | internal/ai | AI provider requests that ended in an error, by provider.
ai_tokens_total | counter | provider, direction | internal/ai | Total AI tokens processed, by provider and direction (input/output).
chat_stream_active | gauge | - | internal/service | Currently in-flight AI chat streams.
go_* | runtime collector | - | internal/metrics | the client library's go collector; its families follow the Go version and the OS
http_request_duration_seconds | histogram | method, route | internal/api/middleware | HTTP request latency by method and normalized route.
http_requests_total | counter | method, route, status | internal/api/middleware | Total HTTP requests processed, labeled by method, normalized route, and status.
pad_advisory_lease_lost_total | counter | - | internal/metrics | Held advisory-lock leases whose heartbeat found the lock gone or the pinned session dead (the database dropped the lock; another replica may take it).
pad_advisory_unlock_not_held_total | counter | - | internal/metrics | Advisory unlocks that reported the lock was not held by the session: the lock was lost while held, or a transaction-mode pooler ran the unlock on another server session (unsupported).
pad_ai_budget_refusals_total | counter | provider, call, reason | internal/ai | AI provider calls refused before they were made, by provider, call (chat, stream, embed; build for a provider the policy refused at the factory) and reason (exceeded, unavailable: the daily AI budget; not_allowed: the deployment or the organisation's allowed-provider list).
pad_ai_hosted_tool_steps_total | counter | provider, tool | internal/ai | Provider-hosted agent tool steps completed (web search, MCP, code interpreter, …), by provider and tool type. Not priced: Azure bills these outside the token usage the daily budget meters.
pad_ai_pricing_fallback_total | counter | provider, model | internal/ai | AI usage priced from provider-default pricing because the model wasn't in the pricing catalog, by provider and model. The model label is a closed set: alias deployments collapse to "deployment" and unknown names to "uncatalogued" (see pricingMetricModel) — raw request models are client-chosen and would mint a series per name.
pad_ai_retry_attempts_total | counter | provider, reason | internal/ai | Retried AI provider attempts (second and later tries), by provider and trigger.
pad_ai_usage_estimated_cost_total | counter | - | internal/ai | Estimated USD cost of AI usage across the deployment. Per-tenant attribution lives in the usage_metrics table (see UsageMetric), which is queryable and does not cost a time series per user.
pad_analysis_runs_total | counter | - | internal/service | Number of analysis runs
pad_audit_dropped_total | counter | reason | internal/audit | Audit events not persisted to the DB (pool full/closed) and diverted to the structured-log fallback sink, by reason.
pad_audit_spill_depth | gauge | - | internal/audit | Audit events currently on the on-disk spill queue (overflow past the in-memory pool). Non-zero means the DB sink fell behind; pair with pad_audit_spill_replayed_total to confirm recovery.
pad_audit_spill_dropped_total | counter | - | internal/audit | Audit events dropped because the on-disk spill queue was at its size cap — only happens under sustained overload beyond the spill capacity.
pad_audit_spill_replayed_total | counter | - | internal/audit | Audit events drained from the on-disk spill queue and re-enqueued to the DB pool.
pad_audit_spilled_total | counter | - | internal/audit | Audit events diverted to the on-disk spill queue because the in-memory pool was full. A reaper drains these back into the DB pool when capacity returns.
pad_auth_operations_total | counter | op | internal/api | Number of auth operations by type
pad_background_dropped_total | counter | task, reason | internal/metrics | Best-effort background tasks (analysis webhooks, finding emails) not started because their concurrency cap was reached or shutdown had begun, by task and reason.
pad_background_inflight | gauge | task | internal/lifecycle | Best-effort background tasks running now, by task. A task pinned at its cap means its target (SMTP, webhook, database) is slow.
pad_background_loop_last_tick_timestamp_seconds | gauge | loop | internal/metrics | Unix timestamp of the last completed iteration of each background loop. Stops updating ⇒ the loop has hung. Pair with pad_background_loop_tick_total to detect deadlocks /healthz cannot see.
pad_background_loop_tick_total | counter | loop | internal/metrics | Iterations of each long-running periodic background loop (scanner, retention_purge). Stops increasing ⇒ the loop has hung. Recommended alert: time() - pad_background_loop_last_tick_timestamp_seconds > 2 * expected_interval. Worker-pool loops (blob_cleaner, audit_pool) are not periodic — they're driven by enqueue — so are not labelled here.
pad_background_task_duration_seconds | histogram | task | internal/lifecycle | Run time of best-effort background tasks, by task.
pad_blob_cleaner_pending | gauge | - | internal/storage/database | Deferred blob-cleanup jobs waiting in the cleaner's pending heap. Sustained growth under bulk import/migration signals the worker pool can't keep up.
pad_blob_content_missing_total | counter | - | internal/storage/database | Flows whose content blob was absent though metadata recorded content — data loss, surfaced so ops can alert rather than only find a log line.
pad_blob_operation_duration_seconds | histogram | op | internal/storage/database | Duration of Azure Blob Storage operations by type
pad_blob_operations_total | counter | op, status | internal/storage/database | Number of Azure Blob Storage operations by type and outcome
pad_cache_cost_bytes | gauge | cache | internal/metrics | Summed cost of the entries held by the declared caches: bytes for byte-budgeted caches; count-bounded caches charge 1 per entry.
pad_cache_entries | gauge | cache | internal/metrics | Entries held by the declared caches (every instance of the cache summed; expired entries count until touched).
pad_cache_evictions_total | counter | cache, reason | internal/metrics | Entries that left the declared caches, by cache and reason: capacity (budget or entry cap), expired (TTL), replaced (stored again under the same key), deleted (invalidated).
pad_cache_requests_total | counter | cache, result | internal/metrics | Lookups of the declared caches, by cache and result: hit, miss, or rejected (the key could not be built, e.g. a missing tenant, so the lookup skipped the cache).
pad_cache_stores_total | counter | cache | internal/metrics | Values stored in the declared caches, by cache. Misses that store nothing were fenced by an invalidation, too large for the cache, or failed.
pad_chat_fix_decisions_total | counter | status | internal/service | apply_fix/apply_fixes approval outcomes by status (applying, applied, applied-unresolved, declined, timeout, cancelled, error) — approval rate, timeouts and failures are observable.
pad_chat_rag_lookups_total | counter | outcome | internal/service | Per-turn knowledge-base guideline lookups by outcome (hit/miss/error/skipped) — RAG health without scraping logs.
pad_chat_tool_iterations_total | counter | - | internal/service | Tool-loop iterations executed (both native and marker-based loops). Sustained growth toward the iteration cap signals models looping without progress.
pad_chat_tool_refused_total | counter | tool, reason | internal/service | Tool calls the session's gate refused before the handler, by tool and reason: scope (a scoped API token without the tool's scope) or approval_unavailable (no approval applier in the session). The model was not offered the tool and called it anyway.
pad_chat_tool_results_total | counter | tool, ok | internal/service | Tool executions by tool and outcome (ok / error) — per-tool reliability and usage at a glance.
pad_ci_webhook_auth_total | counter | method | internal/service | CI webhook calls (POST /api/integrations/ci) that authenticated, by how: key_id (an org CI credential named by X-Baki-Key-Id), global (the deprecated PAD_CI_WEBHOOK_SECRET), flow_org (an org CI credential found through the flow, for bakicli releases that send no key id) or token (a personal API token with the ci scope). global and flow_org should fall to zero before their support is removed.
pad_ci_webhook_deliveries_total | counter | delivery | internal/service | Authenticated CI webhook calls by their deliveryId: new (recorded; the call runs), replayed (already recorded for the same key: 409 CI_REPLAYED, nothing runs) or missing (none sent, a bakicli release before it; accepted). Once missing stays at zero the delivery id can be required.
pad_errors_reported_total | counter | location | internal/errreport | Notable errors forwarded to the error-reporting sink for aggregation/triage, by location.
pad_event_subscriber_duration_seconds | histogram | event, subscriber, tier | internal/platform/eventbus | Run time of one event delivery to one subscriber, by event, subscriber and tier (sync, async).
pad_event_subscriber_failed_total | counter | event, subscriber, reason | internal/platform/eventbus | Event deliveries a subscriber did not complete, by event, subscriber and reason (panic, timeout, dropped: the async runner was saturated or shutting down).
pad_events_published_total | counter | event | internal/platform/eventbus | Domain events published on the in-process event bus, by event.
pad_flow_operations_total | counter | op | internal/service | Number of flow operations by type
pad_job_duration_seconds | histogram | job | internal/metrics | Run time of each background job on this replica, whatever its outcome.
pad_job_last_success_timestamp_seconds | gauge | job | internal/metrics | Unix time of the last successful run of each background job on any replica, as this replica last saw it (its own run, or the persisted job state read when it skipped).
pad_job_overdue | gauge | job | internal/metrics | 1 while a background job has had no successful run on any replica for longer than its overdue threshold (default twice its interval), as this replica saw it at its last attempt; 0 otherwise. Pair with the "job overdue" WARN log line.
pad_job_runs_total | counter | job, outcome | internal/metrics | Runs of each background job on this replica, by outcome: ok, failed, lease_lost (the job's cross-replica lock was lost while it ran; its context was cancelled, or the unlock found the lock gone), panic.
pad_job_skipped_total | counter | job, reason | internal/metrics | Attempts of each background job this replica skipped, by reason: held (another replica, or a run of this one, holds the job's lock: normal on every replica but the holder) or lock_error (the lock could not be asked for; the job fails closed and retries).
pad_library_search_mode_total | counter | mode | internal/service | Cross-library searches by strategy: pushdown (storage-indexed content match) vs scan (in-process, capped at the first 50 flows).
pad_panics_total | counter | location | internal/errreport | Panics recovered (HTTP handlers, background goroutines) forwarded to the error-reporting sink, by location.
pad_rag_dim_mismatch_total | counter | - | internal/rag | Knowledge searches that returned nothing while the org HAS chunks — corpus is stranded at a different embedding dimension than the configured one; re-index.
pad_rag_fallback_capped_total | counter | - | internal/storage/database | Knowledge searches served by the Go-side ranking fallback at its 500-chunk sample cap — chunks beyond the deterministic sample are unsearchable; install pgvector or reduce the KB.
pad_rag_stranded_search_total | counter | - | internal/rag | Knowledge searches that returned nothing while the org has chunks embedded under another embedding identity than the searcher's — a model switch at the same width; re-index.
pad_route_policy_guard_mismatch_total | counter | route | internal/api/middleware | Requests chi dispatched to a different route (or 404/405 fallback) than the one the outer layer resolved and the middleware applied the policy of; answered 500 in declarative mode. Any increase is a resolver bug.
pad_route_policy_mismatch_total | counter | route, decision | internal/api/middleware | Shadow mode (PAD_ROUTE_POLICY=shadow): requests for which the policy declared on the route decides differently from the legacy path tables, by route and decision (auth, scope, ratelimit, tx, deadline). Must stay at zero over a soak before the flip to declarative.
pad_rules_skipped_total | counter | - | internal/service | Rule evaluations aborted via safeCheck's panic recovery (one buggy rule or malformed block); findings may be missing for the affected (block, rule) pairs.
pad_usage_dropped_total | counter | reason | internal/ai | AI usage metrics not recorded and dropped to bound goroutines, by reason: saturated (the wrapper's own slots are busy) or runner (the shared usage runner refused: at its cap or draining; pad_background_dropped_total{task="ai_usage_record"} says which).
pad_ws_connections_active | gauge | - | internal/websocket | Number of active WebSocket connections
pad_ws_inbound_refused_total | counter | type, reason | internal/websocket | WebSocket frames dropped at ingress, by event type (a declared type, or "other") and reason: edit (needs editor rank and the write scope), unknown (not a client-sendable type), invalid (malformed).
postgres_pool_closed_connections | gauge | reason | internal/metrics | Cumulative Postgres connections closed by the pool, by reason: max_idle (idle cap exceeded on return), max_idle_time (ConnMaxIdleTime), max_lifetime (ConnMaxLifetime).
postgres_pool_idle | gauge | - | internal/metrics | Current Postgres connections idle in the pool.
postgres_pool_in_use | gauge | - | internal/metrics | Current Postgres connections checked out of the pool.
postgres_pool_open | gauge | - | internal/metrics | Current total Postgres connections (in use + idle).
postgres_pool_wait_count | gauge | - | internal/metrics | Cumulative number of Postgres connection requests that had to wait for a free pooled connection (database/sql DBStats.WaitCount).
postgres_pool_wait_duration_seconds | gauge | - | internal/metrics | Cumulative time spent waiting for a free pooled Postgres connection (database/sql DBStats.WaitDuration).
process_* | runtime collector | - | internal/metrics | the client library's process collector; its families follow the Go version and the OS
rate_limit_exceeded_total | counter | group | internal/api/middleware | Requests refused by the per-IP rate limiter, by endpoint group.
sse_clients_connected | gauge | - | internal/api | Currently connected Server-Sent Events subscribers.
